{"content":[{"c":["JOANNA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. KJV form of Joanan in ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.27","r":"Luke.3.27","rawR":"Luke.3.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.27","value":"Luke.3.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 3:27"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Joanan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Joanan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Joanan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Joanan"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Wife of Chuza, a steward of Herod the tetrarch. She was among those healed of evil spirits and sickness by Jesus, and contributed to his support (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.8.2-3","r":"Luke.8.2-3","rawR":"Luke.8.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.8.2-3","value":"Luke.8.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 8:2-3"},"). She probably witnessed the Crucifixion and prepared spices for the body; later she found Jesus’ tomb empty (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.23.55-24.10","r":"Luke.23.55-24.10","rawR":"Luke.23.55-24.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.23.55-24.10","value":"Luke.23.55-24.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:55–24:10"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Joanna","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Luke 3:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.3.27","rawQueryValue":"Luke.3.27","sourceRefExact":"Luke.3.27"},{"anchorText":"Lk 8:2-3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.8.2-3","rawQueryValue":"Luke.8.2-3","sourceRefExact":"Luke.8.2-3"},{"anchorText":"23:55–24:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.23.55-24.10","rawQueryValue":"Luke.23.55-24.10","sourceRefExact":"Luke.23.55-24.10"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a2a8196ad44524ff154bee2a9cd6f367654aa4c09735cd2c5fa685a523c49469","sourceItemName"